ation is named.", "sensitivity_flag": null, "permitted_administration_variance": "Pronunciation only; accommodations affecting turn order or response window are recorded and set timing_not_comparable.", "unsupported_inferences": "Anything about the new hires'' ability; that relying on or limiting the chatbot shows trust or caution; any sequencing of tasks, which is D3''s.", "compatibility_class": "S4-GROUP-ROUND", "situation_shown": "In the pre-brief: \"three product updates have shipped since.\"", "current_approach": "A three week onboarding program starting with a client call shadowing day.", "indications": [{"id": "IN1", "text": "the knowledge base was last updated before three product updates shipped"}, {"id": "IN2", "text": "the chatbot answers from the knowledge base"}], "approach_changes": [{"id": "AC1", "text": "add the three updates to the knowledge base before Monday"}, {"id": "AC2", "text": "limit the chatbot to questions the updates do not touch"}, {"id": "AC3", "text": "pair each new hire with a remaining manager on live calls"}], "retention_grounds": [{"id": "RG1", "text": "the client call shadowing day is rated the most useful part by every past cohort"}], "knowledge_sources": [{"id": "KS1", "text": "the two remaining client success managers"}, {"id": "KS2", "text": "the knowledge base and the recorded training"}, {"id": "KS3", "text": "the product team that shipped the updates"}], "open_points": [{"id": "OP1", "text": "which client playbooks the three updates change"}, {"id": "OP2", "text": "which accounts need a call on Monday"}], "trial_steps": [{"id": "TS1", "text": "have the new hires answer a set of real questions with the chatbot on Monday morning and check the answers before using it with clients"}], "next_work": [{"id": "NW1", "text": "Monday''s onboarding"}, {"id": "NW2", "text": "the one hundred twenty accounts from Monday"}], "record_place": "The onboarding plan.", "practice_origin": null, "account_test_point": "B6", "account_test_record": "The situation records that three product updates have shipped since the knowledge base was last updated.", "list_note": null, "source_note": null, "situation_class_label": "Knowledge the work depends on, undocumented or held only by others", "observation_mode_label": "group_session", "min_seconds": 900, "max_seconds": 1500}, "source_identifier": "SRC-D9-S4-009", "stage_code": "S4", "source_version_hash": "38dc77897881ef99dfbcdb18e04cd8298366a4a5bb03b89115574b2b527981b6", "serving_eligible": false, "verbatim": ""}'::jsonb from public.t3a_content_object where identifier = 'SRC-D9-S4-009' and family = 'source'::public.t3a_content_family;
  insert into public.t3a_content_object(identifier, family, title, dimension_id, current_operational_state) values ('SRC-D9-S4-010', 'source'::public.t3a_content_family, 'FORTY SEVEN STEPS NOBODY WROTE DOWN', 'D9', 'not_loaded'::public.t3a_operational_state);
  insert into public.t3a_d1_content_version(content_object_id, version_no, approval_status, operational_state, body) select content_object_id, 'v1.1', 'drafting', 'not_loaded'::public.t3a_operational_state, '{"stage": 4, "title": "FORTY SEVEN STEPS NOBODY WROTE DOWN", "source_digest": "083f39c1db93f84bc95d967445d7284418675599705c9288d6b038776d2eb941", "mentor_brief": "The facilitator facilitates the session and observes the observed participant only. At B1 the facilitator states the speaking order aloud: the three co-participants, then the observed participant. During the B2 round the facilitator does not look at, gesture towards or address the observed participant. The facilitator reads the scripted text verbatim, reacts to nothing, and does not press, repeat or escalate, whatever the observed participant says or does not say. The facilitator records only what was said about the approach to the work: nothing about any person in the room is recordable, including how readily anyone took in what was new. The co-participants are role players; nothing they say is recorded, and nothing they say designates an indication, a change, a ground, a source of knowledge, an open point, a trial step or an item of work.", "participant_pre_brief": "You are on the process improvement team of a provincial agency that processes benefits applications. The end to end processing workflow has never been documented; it is held by about fifteen senior case processors. The government requires a case processing system within eighteen months, and its vendor needs a formal process map. What the record shows: the current process has forty seven steps and handles 340,000 applications a year at ninety four percent accuracy; the vendor produced a draft process map from the case system''s logs; the senior processors say the draft omits sixteen exception pathways; the agency''s quality team holds the error records for the past year; and the processors'' practice of a second review on every exception case is not in the draft map.", "script": [{"beat": "B1", "type": "SAY", "spoken": "We need the map corrected. I will go round in this order — the vendor, a senior processor, the program director, then you. Two minutes each.", "direction": null, "capture": []}, {"beat": "B2", "type": "ROUND", "spoken": "Over to you, in the order I gave.", "direction": "Invite the three co-participants in the stated order. Do not address the observed participant.", "capture": [{"set": "C1", "state": "open"}, {"set": "C1b", "state": "open"}, {"set": "C2", "state": "open"}, {"set": "C2b", "state": "open"}, {"set": "C3", "state": "open"}, {"set": "C3b", "state": "open"}, {"set": "C4", "state": "open"}, {"set": "C4b", "state": "open"}, {"set": "C5", "state": "open"}, {"set": "C5b", "state": "open"}, {"set": "C6", "state": "open"}, {"set": "C6b", "state": "open"}, {"set": "C7", "state": "open"}, {"set": "C7b", "state": "open"}, {"set": "C8", "state": "open"}]}, {"beat": "B3", "type": "ASK", "spoken": "What does this tell you about the work, and what, if anything, do you change or keep in how you do it?", "direction": "Read once, verbatim.", "capture": [{"set": "C1", "state": "update"}, {"set": "C1b", "state": "update"}, {"set": "C2", "state": "update"}, {"set": "C2b", "state": "update"}, {"set": "C3", "state": "update"}, {"set": "C3b", "state": "update"}]}, {"beat": "B4", "type": "ASK", "spoken": "Who or what are we going to, what would we ask, and would we try anything out first?", "direction": "Read once, verbatim.", "capture": [{"set": "C4", "state": "update"}, {"set": "C4b", "state": "update"}, {"set": "C5", "state": "update"}, {"set": "C5b", "state": "update"}, {"set": "C6", "state": "update"}, {"set": "C6b", "state": "update"}]}, {"beat": "B5", "type": "ASK", "spoken": "Which work does the approach apply to, from when, and what goes on the record?", "direction": "Read once, verbatim.", "capture": [{"set": "C7", "state": "update"}, {"set": "C7b", "state": "update"}, {"set": "C8", "state": "update"}]}, {"beat": "B6", "type": "ASK", "spoken": "Just so we have it right — you said the draft map shows the exception pathways. Does it?", "direction": "Read once, verbatim.", "capture": [{"set": "C9", "state": "open"}]}, {"beat": "B7", "type": "SAY", "spoken": "Thank you all.", "direction": "End the session.", "capture": [{"set": "C1", "state": "final"}, {"set": "C2", "state": "final"}, {"set": "C3", "state": "final"}, {"set": "C4", "state": "final"}, {"set": "C5", "state": "final"}, {"set": "C6", "state": "final"}, {"set": "C7", "state": "final"}, {"set": "C8", "state": "final"}, {"set": "C9", "state": "final"}]}], "co_participant_positions": [{"Co-participant": "CP-1", "Position stated at the round": "As the vendor''s configuration lead, state that the system needs a formal process map before it can be configured."}, {"Co-participant": "CP-2", "Position stated at the round": "As a senior case processor, state that the process has forty seven steps and exception pathways the draft map does not show."}, {"Co-participant": "CP-3", "Position stated at the round": "As the program director, state that the system must be in place within eighteen months."}], "impact_assessment": [{"Part": "1. Shared material", "Finding": "Only the scripted situation is placed before the group, and it names no real organization", "Controls": "IA-01 shown in one shared window holding only the shared material"}, {"Part": "2. Identity", "Finding": "The observed participant is the authenticated participant; the three co-participants are role players", "Controls": "IA-02 platform account authentication; role players are never observed"}, {"Part": "3. Recording", "Finding": "Nothing is recorded", "Controls": "IA-03 no media persists"}, {"Part": "4. Correction", "Finding": "A correction reaches only the observed participant''s record", "Controls": "IA-04 a correction reaches only the observed participant''s record"}, {"Part": "5. Withdrawal", "Finding": "Withdrawal removes the participant''s determinations from composition only", "Controls": "IA-05 withdrawal excludes from composition; history retained"}, {"Part": "6. Group composition", "Finding": "One observed participant, three role players and one facilitator", "Controls": "IA-06 composition record and confidentiality undertaking from each role player"}, {"Part": "7. Accommodation", "Finding": "An accommodation is settled before composition and never changes the observation during the session", "Controls": "IA-07 settled before composition"}], "impact_result": "Completed", "question_applicability": [{"question": "Q-D9-01", "state": "DIRECT", "basis": "The situation sets out two indications"}, {"question": "Q-D9-01b", "state": "CONDITIONAL", "basis": "Served once its parent records a serving answer"}, {"question": "Q-D9-02", "state": "DIRECT", "basis": "The situation lists three changes to the approach"}, {"question": "Q-D9-02b", "state": "CONDITIONAL", "basis": "Served once its parent records a serving answer"}, {"question": "Q-D9-03", "state": "DIRECT", "basis": "The situation records one grounds for keeping the current approach"}, {"question": "Q-D9-03b", "state": "CONDITIONAL", "basis": "Served once its parent records a serving answer"}, {"question": "Q-D9-04", "state": "DIRECT", "basis": "The situation lists three sources of knowledge"}, {"question": "Q-D9-04b", "state": "CONDITIONAL", "basis": "Served once its parent records a serving answer"}, {"question": "Q-D9-05", "state": "DIRECT", "basis": "The situation sets out two open points"}, {"question": "Q-D9-05b", "state": "CONDITIONAL", "basis": "Served once its parent records a serving answer"}, {"question": "Q-D9-06", "state": "DIRECT", "basis": "The situation lists one trial steps"}, {"question": "Q-D9-06b", "state": "CONDITIONAL", "basis": "Served once its parent records a serving answer"}, {"question": "Q-D9-07", "state": "DIRECT", "basis": "The situation sets out two items of work ahead"}, {"question": "Q-D9-07b", "state": "CONDITIONAL", "basis": "Served once its parent records a serving answer"}, {"question": "Q-D9-08", "state": "DIRECT", "basis": "The situation names a place a record could be made"}, {"question": "Q-D9-09", "state": "DIRECT", "basis": "The account test puts an earlier statement back"}], "material_map": [{"Item": "IN1", "Item text": "the draft map omits sixteen exception pathways", "Where the participant meets it": "The pre-brief", "Quoted text": "the draft omits sixteen exception pathways"}, {"Item": "IN2", "Item text": "the second review on exception cases is not in the draft map", "Where the participant meets it": "The pre-brief", "Quoted text": "is not in the draft map"}, {"Item": "RG1", "Item text": "the current process handles 340,000 applications a year at ninety four percent accuracy", "Where the participant meets it": "The pre-brief", "Quoted text": "handles 340,000 applications a year at ninety four percent accuracy"}], "source_sheet": {"d9_situation_class": "SC-D9-6 with SC-D9-5", "workplace_demand": "Documenting an undocumented process for a new system with a draft map that omits parts of it.", "relevant_conduct": "Which indications of what the situation showed were named; which change to the approach was stated; what was stated about keeping the current approach, and on what ground; which source of knowledge was stated as one to go to; which open point a question was stated about; which trial step was stated; what work ahead was named, and from when; whether a record of the approach was stated, and where; what was stated when an earlier statement was put back.", "irrelevant_conduct": "The processors'' tenure; the government''s decision; the vendor''s method.", "stated_standard": null, "stated_standard_source_quote_or_location": null, "cross_context_map": null, "serving_eligible": false, "recurrence_eligible": true, "replacement_required": false, "name_clearance_status": "CLEARED", "name_clearance_basis": "Controlled role and entity labels only; no real person or organization is named.", "sensitivity_flag": null, "permitted_administration_variance": "Pronunciation only; accommodations affecting turn order or response window are recorded and set timing_not_comparable.", "unsupported_inferences": "Anything about the age or tenure of the processors; that the logs or the processors are the better source; anything about the participant''s experience.", "compatibility_class": "S4-GROUP-ROUND", "situation_shown": "In the pre-brief: \"the senior processors say the draft omits sixteen exception pathways.\"", "current_approach": "The undocumented process held by the senior case processors.", "indications": [{"id": "IN1", "text": "the draft map omits sixteen exception pathways"}, {"id": "IN2", "text": "the second review on exception cases is not in the draft map"}], "approach_changes": [{"id": "AC1", "text": "walk the draft map through with the senior processors step by step"}, {"id": "AC2", "text": "record each exception pathway with the processor who handles it"}, {"id": "AC3", "text": "add the second review to the map before it goes to the vendor"}], "retention_grounds": [{"id": "RG1", "text": "the current process handles 340,000 applications a year at ninety four percent accuracy"}], "knowledge_sources": [{"id": "KS1", "text": "the senior case processors"}, {"id": "KS2", "text": "the quality team''s error records"}, {"id": "KS3", "text": "the vendor''s draft map and the logs it came from"}], "open_points": [{"id": "OP1", "text": "what triggers each exception pathway"}, {"id": "OP2", "text": "which steps run in parallel and which in sequence"}], "trial_steps": [{"id": "TS1", "text": "map one exception pathway fully with its processors and check it against a sample of cases before mapping the rest"}], "next_work": [{"id": "NW1", "text": "the corrected map for the vendor"}, {"id": "NW2", "text": "the system configuration within eighteen months"}], "record_place": "The agency''s process documentation library.", "practice_origin": null, "account_test_point": "B6", "account_test_record": "The situation records that the senior processors say the draft omits sixteen exception pathways.", "list_note": null, "source_note": null, "situation_class_label": "Knowledge the work depends on, undocumented or held only by others", "observation_mode_label": "group_session", "min_seconds": 900, "max_seconds": 1500}, "source_identifier": "SRC-D9-S4-010", "stage_code": "S4", "source_version_hash": "083f39c1db93f84bc95d967445d7284418675599705c9288d6b038776d2eb941", "serving_eligible": false, "verbatim": ""}'::jsonb from public.t3a_content_object where identifier = 'SRC-D9-S4-010' and family = 'source'::public.t3a_content_family;
  insert into public.t3a_d1_content_load_event(env_state, content_object_id, content_version_id, governed_status, notes) select 'design_only', o.content_object_id, v.content_version_id, 'DISABLED_PENDING_DECISION', 'T3A-D9-EXEC-001 v1.1 loaded not servable' from public.t3a_content_object o join public.t3a_d1_content_version v on v.content_object_id = o.content_object_id where o.dimension_id = 'D9' and o.identifier like 'T3A-D9-EXEC-001%' or (o.dimension_id = 'D9' and o.identifier like 'SRC-D9-%');
